Thank you for the almost instant responses, especially those from Bill
Dunlap and Jean Adams.  Both pointed out that the "z" argument for persp
needs to be a matrix, I was providing a vector.

In my case Bill Dunlap's solution was the easiest to implement, i.e. insert

wan.surf <- array(wan.surf, c(41,41))

which converted my vector to the appropriate matrix, and run 

persp(Cl,Cd.d,wan.surf)

again.

It worked like a charm.

